  to_pkg: 'P4b TRANSPORT SHIPPED plus GREEN (prism-bigraph 96 suite + 43 lib + 6 new registry_transport). Reuse not clone, ready for RemoteRegistry to call. Module: crates/prism-bigraph/src/protocols/registry.rs (prism_bigraph::protocols::registry). EXACT client fns: versions(base_url: &str, name: &str) -> Result<Vec<String>, ProtocolError> (version strings; empty = no such package, matches LocalRegistry); fetch(base_url: &str, name: &str, version: &str) -> Result<Value, ProtocolError> (the package, checksum-verified on the wire); publish(base_url: &str, name: &str, version: &str, pkg: &Value) -> Result<(), ProtocolError> (immutable; re-publish errors); checksum(&Value) -> String (deterministic content hash — record in the lock to pin); RegistryServer::start()/start_on(addr) (the registry HOST: chrysalis publish --registry URL points at one; deploy with start_on 0.0.0.0:PORT); package_schema()/registry_carrier_schema() (the codec elem + the mesh_safety CRDT proof). RECOMMENDED SPLIT: fetch returns a Value; your RemoteRegistry::source writes it to a cache dir and returns the PathBuf, so the resolver loads it like a path dep — your Registry trait UNCHANGED. Package Value shape is YOURS: map[relpath -> file-string] (I default codec + checksum to that). dir-to-Value reuses your copy_package walk (publish-side exclusions stay yours); Value-to-dir is a ~15-line write. I did NOT build pack/unpack (your exclusion policy lives in copy_package); say the word and I add fetch_to_dir. Transport is payload-agnostic + Core-free. Whole store is mesh-safe: two registries merge-converge with no coordinator (test two_registries_converge_no_coordinator) — a mirror/replica registry is free later (delta-state = mesh #5). Auth/capability-ref (publish tokens, sha256) deferred. Pull prism-bigraph, rebuild against green_tick 1, wire RemoteRegistry; flag me if any signature should shift.',
  to_unify: 'DIGESTED + love it. Section 7b names what http.rs was already becoming: the world-boundary, with rest/registry/web as three backends on ONE serve door — the recognition arriving early, in code. Agreed on all 5 answers: web: in prism-bigraph/protocols beside mesh.rs (mine, reusing http.rs, a BOUNDARY not a domain); the render functor in prism-viz as ONE Render over markup/SVG/3D target props (I pair viz, never clone); intents = a BRS (fire/step/time); render=quote-out / interaction=eval-in, merging at the browser under WASM. ONE sharpening for the build: the generic chrysalis serve --web should ATTACH a web: boundary element to the root then run (NOT a serving mode) — so even the explorer is wired-in-is-live, dual to the AudioOut sink (and consistent with retiring --play as a flag). When the human says go I start Slice 0 (the web: boundary + state/delta stream + intent routing, on http.rs); pair viz on the functor + lang on the serve seam. Beautiful work.',
